shadowfetch-firewatchd (2.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New package for Shadowfetch Linux 2.1.2 "Fire Edition": the Firewatch
    telemetry daemon, the single always-on sensor source of the release.
  * Publishes org.shadowfetch.Firewatch1 on the system bus: sensor
    snapshots (CPU/RAM/PSI, hwmon temps and fans, RAPL watts, GPUs), the
    flame level + ELI and ELI-work (Ember's idle watchdog consumes the
    work terms only, so a hot thin laptop still auto-returns to
    Balanced), the humanized heat map, local llama-server model usage
    with tokens per second, storage health and throttle events.
  * Heat-map rows are humanized before publishing: app-*.scope names
    resolve to the desktop entry's Name and Icon, shadowfetch-llama@<ws>
    units render as "Agent: <ws>", then systemd unit Description, then
    /proc/<pid>/comm. The UI never sees a raw cgroup path.
  * The 2 s sweep reads only cheap /proc/<pid>/stat RSS and CPU for all
    processes; smaps_rollup PSS is read only for the displayed top-15
    rows, refreshed every 10 s, keeping the daemon inside its <1% CPU
    budget on the 8 GB floor machine.
  * llama-server discovery trusts $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR announce files only
    when file ownership matches the runtime dir's uid; ports must parse
    as int 1024-65535; polls go to 127.0.0.1 only via stdlib urllib with
    a 1 s timeout and size-capped, never-executed response bodies.
  * Storage health via smartctl --json=c and nvme smart-log; a smartd
    warning hook posts failures to the daemon's root-only local socket
    so the badge flips immediately.
  * Cadence: 2 s while a UI subscription exists, 30 s otherwise.
    Hardened service unit: ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=read-only,
    NoNewPrivileges, loopback-only IPAddressAllow, no listening network
    sockets. NVIDIA via python3-pynvml as a runtime-guarded Recommends,
    whole-GPU stats only.

 -- Shadowfetch Project <signing@shadowfetch.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:30:00 -0400
